msgid "gRPC code generation reference guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This reference guide explains how to configure gRPC code generation. It is "
"recommended to read the xref:grpc.adoc[official gRPC guide] first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enabling gRPC code generation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, `\\*.proto` files located in the `src/main/proto` directory are "
"compiled into Java sources during the build process."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using Maven"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable gRPC code generation, add the following dependency to your project:"
""
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus:generate-code` goal is executed by default during the Quarkus "
"Maven plugin default lifecycle when using the `quarkus` packaging,\n"
"and will handle the code generation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Using Gradle"
msgstr ""

msgid "For Gradle, add the following dependency to your project:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Customizing the <em>proto</em> directory"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, it is assumed that the `\\*.proto` files are located in the `src/"
"main/proto` directory.\n"
"You can configure this location using the `quarkus.grpc.codegen.proto-"
"directory` property in your **build descriptor**."
msgstr ""

msgid "With Maven, add the following configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "With Gradle, use the following configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generating Descriptor Set"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Protocol Buffers do not contain descriptions of their own types. Thus, given "
"only a raw message without the corresponding .proto file defining its type, "
"it is difficult to extract any useful data. However, the contents of a ."
"proto file can itself be https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/techniques/"
"#self-description[represented using protocol buffers]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, Quarkus does not generate these descriptors. Quarkus does "
"provide several configuration options for generating them. These would be "
"added to your `application.properties` or `application.yml` file:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.generate-code.grpc.descriptor-set.generate`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Set to `true` to enable generation"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.generate-code.grpc.descriptor-set.output-dir`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Set this to a value relative to the project's build directory (i.e. `target` "
"for Maven, `build` for Gradle)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Maven default value: `target/generated-sources/grpc`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Gradle default value: `$buildDir/classes/java/quarkus-generated-sources/"
"grpc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "`quarkus.generate-code.grpc.descriptor-set.name`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Name of the descriptor set file to generate"
msgstr ""

msgid "Default value: `descriptor_set.dsc`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Configuring gRPC code generation for dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You may have dependencies that contain `\\*.proto` files you want to compile "
"to Java sources.\n"
"This section explains how to configure code generation to include these `\\*."
"proto` files during code generation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Proto files for imports"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Protocol Buffers specification provides a way to import `proto` files.\n"
"The Quarkus code generation mechanism lets you control the scope of "
"dependencies to scan for possible imports by setting the `quarkus.generate-"
"code.grpc.scan-for-imports` property in your `application.properties`.\n"
"You can set it to one of the following values:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`all` - scan all dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`none` - don't scan dependencies, use only what is defined in `src/main/"
"proto` or `src/test/proto`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`groupId1:artifactId1,groupId2:artifactId2` - scan only the specified "
"dependencies by group ID and artifact ID."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If not specified, the property defaults to `com.google.protobuf:protobuf-"
"java`.\n"
"To override it, set the `quarkus.generate-code.grpc.scan-for-imports` "
"property in your `application.properties`.\n"
"For example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Proto files from dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In some cases, you may want to use `proto` files from a different project to "
"generate gRPC stubs.\n"
"To do this:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Add a dependency on the artifact that contains the proto file to your "
"project."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In `application.properties`, specify the dependencies you want to scan for "
"proto files."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The value of the property can be `none`, which is the default, or a comma-"
"separated list of `groupId:artifactId` coordinates."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the dependency contains many proto files, and you want to generate "
"classes for only a subset of them, you can specify glob patterns per "
"dependency.\n"
"The paths to match are relative to the `src/main/resources` path in the "
"dependency. For example:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Note that `:` characters in the property keys must be escaped."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kotlin code generation"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"`protoc` also supports https://protobuf.dev/reference/kotlin/kotlin-"
"generated/[generating Kotlin code] in addition to the generated Java code."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"By default, the Kotlin code generation is enabled if the dependency `io."
"quarkus:quarkus-kotlin` is present."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To explicitly en-/disable this feature, set the `quarkus.generate-code.grpc."
"kotlin.generate` property in your `application.properties` file to `true` or "
"`false`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Skipping code generation"
msgstr ""

msgid "You can skip gRPC code generation using:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The `grpc.codegen.skip` system property: `-Dgrpc.codegen.skip=true`"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `quarkus.grpc.codegen.skip` property in your `application.properties` "
"file: `quarkus.grpc.codegen.skip=true`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Generating Java files from proto with the protobuf-maven-plugin"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Alternatively, to generate stubs for `proto` files, you can use the "
"`protobuf-maven-plugin`.\n"
"However, it's recommended to use Quarkus support unless you have a specific "
"need."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To do this, define the following properties in the `<properties>` section:"
msgstr ""

msgid "These properties configure the gRPC version and the `protoc` version."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Then, add the `eu.maveniverse.maven.nisse:plugin3` and the `protobuf-maven-"
"plugin` configuration to the `build` section:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `protobuf-maven-plugin` generates stub classes from your gRPC service "
"definition (`proto` files)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Class generation uses the tool `protoc`, which is OS-specific. This is why "
"we use the Nisse Maven plugin to target the executable compatible with the "
"operating system."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Note: This configuration instructs the `protobuf-maven-plugin` to generate "
"default gRPC classes and classes using Mutiny to fit with the Quarkus "
"development experience."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In order for the Nisse Maven plugin to generate the correct properties, we "
"need to make sure the `nisse.compat.osDetector` system\n"
"property is set. This can be done by adding the following `.mvn/maven."
"config` file:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Using generated gRPC classes from dependencies"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When gRPC classes, which are classes generated from `proto` files, are in a "
"dependency of the application, the dependency needs a Jandex index.\n"
"You can create a Jandex index using the `jandex-maven-plugin`.\n"
"More information on this topic can be found in the xref:cdi-reference."
"adoc#bean_discovery[Bean Discovery] section of the CDI guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you are using Gradle, you can use the following configuration:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Argument files"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When the `protoc` command line exceeds the maximum command length, you can "
"ask Quarkus to use an argument file to pass the arguments to the `protoc` "
"command."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To enable this feature, set the `quarkus.generate-code.grpc.use-arg-file` "
"property in your `application.properties` file to `true`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are on Windows, and the command line exceeds 8190 characters, Quarkus "
"automatically uses an argument file to pass the arguments to the `protoc` "
"command."
msgstr ""

msgid "Local vs. Downloaded <code>protoc</code>"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To generate gRPC classes, Quarkus uses the `protoc` artifact from the `com."
"google.protobuf` group id.\n"
"However, to ensure the support of various platforms, Quarkus automatically "
"downloads _all_ the possible variants of the `protoc` artifact.\n"
"In addition, Quarkus downloads both `protoc` and the plugin used to generate "
"gRPC classes in Java.\n"
"For example, even if you are using Linux, Quarkus downloads the `protoc` and "
"the Java plugin artifacts for Windows and MacOS."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The next table lists the different variants of the `protoc` and plugin "
"artifacts:"
msgstr ""

